{"availability":"available","full":"tecnickcom/TCPDF","name":"TCPDF","description":"Deprecated: PHP PDF library, superseded by tc-lib-pdf (https://github.com/tecnickcom/tc-lib-pdf)","category":"Other","language":"PHP","stars":4528,"forks":1577,"created":"2014-08-08T08:49:17Z","updated":"2026-10-03T13:00:25Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://tcpdf.org","topics":["pdf","pdf-generation"],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","stars":4528,"forks":1577}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["TCPDF is in maintenance-only mode. Active development has moved to tc-lib-pdf, its modern, modular successor — new projects should start there. TCPDF is still installed 100M+ times across 500+ PHP packages. If your product depends on it, sponsor continued maintenance → to keep this shared infrastructure secure and patched.","TCPDF is a pure-PHP library for generating PDF documents and barcodes directly in application code.","It has been widely used across many PHP stacks and still provides a complete feature set for text rendering, page composition, graphics, signatures, forms, and standards-oriented output."],"features":["Larger feature set: tc-lib-pdf offers many more features than TCPDF, and it is where new ones are added.","Modern architecture: modular libraries and cleaner component boundaries improve maintainability.","Better extensibility: new features are easier to add without patching a monolithic legacy core.","Stronger tooling fit: modern package structure works better with static analysis, CI, and automated tests.","Lower long-term risk: reduces technical debt tied to legacy APIs and supports ongoing PHP ecosystem evolution."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tecnickcom/TCPDF/